      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1842, the governor of Kauai leased Princeville’s Crown Lands for a coffee plantation, and Robert Crichton Wyllie bought the lease in 1853.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princeville%2C_Hawaii",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After acquiring the lease, Wyllie planted Princeville’s land with sugarcane, shifting the area from coffee to a major sugar industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princeville%2C_Hawaii",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1852, the first Chinese contract laborers arrived on Princeville to work in the island’s burgeoning sugar plantations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
